'aba-therapy':{rel:['workshops','hire-an-lsa'],e:'Therapy session',h:'ABA Therapy <em>in your child’s world</em>',tl:'Support that meets your child where they are.',lead:'We bring expert Applied Behaviour Analysis therapy directly into your home. It’s a compassionate, evidence-based approach that helps children build meaningful skills in the place they feel most comfortable.',img:'a2',form:'aba',ft:'Make an enquiry',fp:'Fill in the form below and our team will be in touch within 48 hours for a free, no-obligation consultation.',
b:[{y:'text',t:'What is ABA therapy?',p:['Applied Behaviour Analysis (ABA) is a structured, play-based approach to therapy that focuses on understanding how behaviour works and using that understanding to increase helpful behaviours and reduce those that affect a child’s quality of life.','It is widely used to support children with autism spectrum disorder (ASD), ADHD, and other developmental differences. It helps them develop communication, social, self-care, and learning skills in a positive, rewarding environment.']},
{y:'cards',t:'Why choose home-based ABA?',p:'Delivering therapy in your home offers real advantages for your child’s learning and wellbeing.',c:[['In the comfort of home','Sessions take place in your child’s own environment, where they feel safest and most at ease. This familiarity helps skills generalise naturally into everyday life.'],['Evidence-based practice','ABA is one of the most thoroughly researched interventions for autism and developmental differences, with decades of proven outcomes.'],['Child-led and compassionate','Our therapists build genuine relationships with each child. Sessions are warm, positive, and motivating, never mechanical or repetitive.'],['Family involvement','We work with the whole family, not just the child. Parents and carers receive guidance so progress made in sessions continues throughout the day.'],['Fully qualified therapists','Every therapist is trained, supervised, and experienced in delivering ABA therapy with children across a range of needs and ages.'],['Flexible scheduling','Sessions are arranged around your family’s routine, in the mornings, afternoons, or evenings, at a frequency that suits your child’s programme.']]},
{y:'steps',t:'What to expect',p:'From first contact to ongoing sessions, here’s how it works.',s:[['Initial assessment','We start with a thorough assessment of your child’s current skills, goals, and interests to create a personalised ABA programme.'],['Matched therapist','We carefully match your child with the therapist best suited to their personality, needs, and goals.'],['Home sessions begin','Therapy begins in your home with structured yet playful sessions, building skills step by step.'],['Regular review and progress reports','We review goals regularly and keep you informed with clear progress updates so you always see how your child is developing.']]},
{y:'quote',t:'Every child deserves to be understood and supported.',p:'We take the time to truly know your child, their strengths, their challenges, and what makes them smile, so that every session feels purposeful and kind.'}]},

