const FAQ=[
['Do we need a diagnosis to get support?','No. Support is based on what your child is finding hard, not on a label. If you do have a diagnosis or report, it helps us plan, so share it if you’re comfortable.'],
['What happens in the free intro consultation?','We talk about your goals and concerns, answer your questions, and suggest a first step. There is no pressure to continue.'],
['What is the difference between a consultation and a therapy session?','A consultation is a 60-minute session of advice and planning, for example on literacy, behaviour, or learning strategies. Therapy sessions (ABA, speech, and occupational therapy) are ongoing, hands-on support for your child. If you’re unsure, start with the free 20-minute intro consultation.'],
['How much do sessions cost?','Your intro consultation is free. For other consultations and therapy sessions, we share pricing after your free consultation so the plan fits your child’s needs.'],
['Who are the workshops for?','Parents and carers, learning support assistants, teachers, SENCOs, and school leaders. We can also tailor a workshop to your school or group.'],
['Can parents or guardians join sessions?','Yes. For younger learners we work with the whole family, and we agree together how you’ll be involved.'],
['How do I hire a learning support assistant?','Use the Hire a Learning Support Assistant form and choose parent or school enquiry. We’ll arrange a consultation, match you with a suitable LSA, and arrange trial sessions.'],
['How do I apply to join your team?','Go to the Careers page, fill in the form, and attach your CV. We’ll be in touch.'],
['What happens after I send an enquiry?','We reply within 48 hours by email or WhatsApp to arrange your free consultation or confirm your requested time.'],
['How do I cancel or reschedule?','Message us on WhatsApp or by email as early as you can and we’ll find a new time.']];
const GU=[
{t:'Build a study plan that sticks',s:'A simple routine beats a perfect plan.',p:['Pick a fixed start time and place.','Work in short blocks, such as 20 minutes, then rest for 5.','Write down the next small step, not the whole task.','Review the plan each Sunday and adjust it.']},
{t:'Supporting reading at home',s:'Little and often builds confident readers.',p:['Read together for 10 minutes a day, in a quiet spot.','Let your child choose books about things they love.','Pause to talk about the story and new words.','Praise effort, and return to the same book for fluency.']},
{t:'Positive behaviour strategies at home',s:'Behaviour is communication. Look for what it is telling you.',p:['Note what happens before and after the behaviour.','Teach a simple, positive alternative, such as asking for a break.','Praise the new behaviour straight away and often.','Stay calm, consistent, and keep routines predictable.']},
{t:'Choosing assistive technology',s:'Match the tool to the barrier, not the other way round.',p:['Name the barrier: reading, writing, focus, or organizing.','Try one free tool first, such as text-to-speech or dictation.','Test it for a week on real homework.','Keep what helps and drop what doesn’t.']},
{t:'Asking for school accommodations',s:'Clear, specific requests are easier to approve.',p:['Note what helps your learner and what gets in the way.','Collect examples, reports, or teacher comments.','Write each request in one plain sentence.','Bring a short summary to the meeting and ask for next steps in writing.']},
{t:'Building life skills at home',s:'Small, repeated practice builds independence.',p:['Choose one skill, such as packing a school bag.','Break it into 3 to 5 steps and show each one.','Use a picture or checklist to prompt, then fade it.','Praise effort and celebrate each step done alone.']}];
